---
globs: src/tools/**
alwaysApply: false
---

Read `.cursor/skills/add-agent-tool/SKILL.md` before changing a tool.

- Tool arguments reach `execute` as untyped, trimmed strings, because the model emits XML. Coerce
  and validate every one.
- The return value is fed straight back into a 0.8B model's context. Keep it compact and cap
  anything that could be unbounded.
- There is an optional proxy in `tools/agent-api.ts`. A tool that needs the network must still work
  from the tab against an endpoint that sends CORS headers, in `src/tools/web.ts`, or it cannot run
  on the hosted site. DuckDuckGo search and `read_page` may *also* go through `/api` when a proxy is
  configured — that is not licence to add a tool that only works there.
- A new tool needs a scenario in `src/eval/scenarios.ts`, or nothing measures whether the model
  actually routes to it.
